Fixes: f248d5d5159a ("drm/msm/a6xx: Fix PDC sleep sequence")

PENDING, NOT APPLIED.  This file lives in kernel/patches/pending/, which
scripts/prepare-kernel.sh ignores, so no build carries it today.  It is kept here
so the candidate is frozen, reviewable and hashable rather than living in a chat.

Upstream status (checked 2026-09-25):
  series   [PATCH 0/6] drm/msm: Assorted fixes - June/26, v1
  patch    1/6
  latest   v1 - no v2 exists; replies from Neil Armstrong, Dmitry Baryshkov,
           Konrad Dybcio
  base     ef8274b9c19a4b614e10ce95553d0d363dc1c1f8
  lore     https://lore.kernel.org/lkml/20260605-assorted-fixes-june-v1-1-2caa04f7287c@oss.qualcomm.com/
  patchew  https://patchew.org/linux/20260605-assorted-fixes-june-v1-0-2caa04f7287c@oss.qualcomm.com/

Why X710 needs it:
  The condition is inverted in the pinned v7.2-rc3, so a6xx_rpmh_stop() returns
  early whenever GMU_STATUS_FW_START was set - the normal case - and the whole
  RSCC power-off handshake is skipped:
    REG_A6XX_GMU_RSCC_CONTROL_REQ=1, the RSCC status poll, the request clear, and
    set_bit(GMU_STATUS_PDC_SLEEP).
  It is reached from every GPU runtime suspend:
    a6xx_gmu_pm_suspend() -> a6xx_gmu_stop() -> {a6xx_gmu_shutdown() |
    a6xx_gmu_force_off()} -> a6xx_rpmh_stop().
  The GPU binds on X710 only since the round-15 AOSS QMP + IPCC fix, so this path
  was dead code on this board until then.  Upstream's own words for the effect:
  "There are stale RPMH votes (BCM votes) observed after GMU suspend. This is
  because the rpmh stop sequences are skipped during gmu suspend."

  This is an upstream bugfix, not an X710-specific hack.  The inverted line is in
  the committed v7.2-rc3 tree (`git show HEAD:drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/
  a6xx_gmu.c`); this repository's only other change to that file is 0007, which
  touches the two device_link_add() calls at lines 2238 and 2425.

Backport adaptation (recorded because the series is one revision ahead of nothing
but its own base commit):
  Hunk 2 of the upstream patch writes REG_A6XX_GMU_CM3_SYSRESET before
  a6xx_rpmh_stop() in a6xx_gmu_shutdown().  The pinned tree ALREADY has that write
  at a6xx_gmu.c:1158, in a later upstream form (with bus_halt and
  a6xx_gpu_sw_reset in between).  So only hunk 1 is carried: one line.
  Nothing else is adapted; the hunk-1 context matches the pinned tree exactly.

Not a fix claim: the upstream commit reports stale votes, not hangs.  Nothing yet
connects a stale BCM vote to a CPU that stops answering an ordinary IPI.  See
docs/A6XX_STALE_RPMH_VOTES.md sections 5 and 6, including the read-only on-device
checks that must be done BEFORE a rebuild - if the GPU never autosuspends on this
board, the defect cannot bite and this lead closes.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
@@ -642,7 +642,7 @@ static void a6xx_rpmh_stop(struct a6xx_gmu *gmu)
 	int ret;
 	u32 val;
 
-	if (test_and_clear_bit(GMU_STATUS_FW_START, &gmu->status))
+	if (!test_and_clear_bit(GMU_STATUS_FW_START, &gmu->status))
 		return;
 
 	if (adreno_is_a840(adreno_gpu))
